  "notes": "USAGE:\nFocuses on visible changes in appearance due to aging. Can be blunt or even rude when said directly to someone. The past form {老|ふ}けた is often used as a modifier meaning \"aged-looking.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {老|ふ}けて⟦{見|み}える→見える：01165_mieru⟧ (to look old)\n- ⟦すっかり→すっかり：01270_sukkari⟧{老|ふ}ける (to age completely)\n- ⟦{急|きゅう}→急：13042_kyuu⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{老|ふ}ける (to age suddenly)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{年|とし}→年：00486_toshi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{取|と}る→取る：00565_toru⟧: to grow older — neutral and objective\n- ⟦{老|お}いる→老いる：04582_oiru⟧: to grow old — more literary, focuses on the process of aging itself",
